course: dictionary
lesson: 8297
title: One word, two meanings: river
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A river is a large stream of fresh water that flows across land to a lake, another river or the sea. You can see rivers on maps as long blue lines.
explain: The word river has a second meaning too. A river of something is a large flowing amount. «A river of lava» is not water at all: it means a huge amount of lava flowing like water, so the word tells you how much and how it moves.
explain: Context shows you which meaning to use. Look for the words around the word. When you see «rivers» beside «ponds, lakes and canals», it is the water meaning. When you see «lava» or «tears», it is the flowing amount.
fact: A river is a large stream of fresh water that flows across land.
fact: Rivers flow to a lake, another river or the sea.
fact: The source is where a river starts, and the mouth is where it ends.
fact: A tributary is a smaller river that flows into a bigger river.
fact: «A river of lava» means a large flowing amount of lava.
fact: Rivers can be deep and fast, so swim only in safe places where a grown-up is watching.
exercise: According to «The advice of RoSPA is never to go onto ice on ponds, lakes, rivers or canals», what should people never walk on in winter? | Fresh snow in the garden | Wooden bridges over paths | Sandy beaches | *Ice on ponds, lakes, rivers or canals
exercise: What does river mean in «a river of lava»? | A stream of fresh water to the sea | A road beside the sea | *A large flowing amount | A kind of boat
exercise: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat pushed along with a long pole on shallow rivers.» Where is a punt used? | On the open sea in a storm | Under the ground | *On shallow rivers | On the top of a mountain
test: Which sentence about a river is correct? | A river is a kind of bird that lives in trees | *A river is a large stream of fresh water that flows across land | A river is always salty like the sea | A river is a tall hill made of rock
test: The place where a river ends, by flowing into a lake or the sea, is called its what? | The source | The bank | *The mouth | The tributary
exam: «Imagine being so slow that green algae grow in your hair, then remember that the same sloth can swim across a river about three times faster than it climbs.» Why is it a good idea to swim only in safe, watched places in a river? | *Rivers can be deep and fast, and it is dangerous to swim in them alone | Rivers stop flowing in the summer | Rivers are always warm and calm | Rivers are made of ice and only freeze
